# payment is allowed to this origin and PayPal only. It used to be blanket-denied, which is the
# wrong default for the one page on the site whose whole purpose is taking a payment. The standard
# PayPal button uses a popup and does not need it, but Venmo and the card fields do, and a
# checkout that silently half-works is worse than one that never appears.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=(self "https://www.paypal.com")
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains

# The dashboard shows a licence and a paid download. Nothing here should be cached by a
# shared proxy, and it should not be indexed.
#
# Matched on /account, not /account.html: Workers Assets canonicalises the extension away and
# redirects, so a rule written against the .html only ever decorated the redirect and never
# the page anyone actually loads. Both are listed so it holds either way.
/account
  Cache-Control: no-store
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex

/account.html
  Cache-Control: no-store
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
